 "result": "I created `Dockerfile` and `.dockerignore` in the repository root. I did not modify any existing files. I couldn't build or run the image here, so it's untested.\n\n- **`Dockerfile`** has three stages:\n  - **Frontend:** builds the Vite dashboard with `npm ci` and `npm run build`. The API base URL is left empty, which matches the code's same-origin default.\n  - **Python:** installs `requirements.txt` into a virtualenv on `python:3.12-slim-bookworm`.\n  - **Runtime:** copies the virtualenv, `src/`, `config/`, `config.yaml`, `models/` and the built `frontend/dist`. It runs as a non-root user and exposes port 8000. The health check hits `/api/health`, and the start command matches `run_api.sh` (`uvicorn ... --workers 1`).\n- **`.dockerignore`** excludes VCS and editor files, virtualenvs, `node_modules`, `.env` files, secrets, and runtime data such as `outputs/`, `logs/` and `data/`. It keeps `package.json` and the lockfile, which the frontend build needs.\n\nChoices I made that you may want to change:\n- **No `pip install -e .`:** the image sets `PYTHONPATH=/app/src` instead. `config.py` derives the project root from the package location, so `/app` resolves correctly this way. Nothing reads installed package metadata.\n- **`DATABASE_URL`** defaults to `/app/outputs/climatevision.sqlite3`. Mount a volume at `/app/outputs` to keep runs across restarts.\n- **Installs the full `requirements.txt`:** this includes Jupyter, pytest and other dev tools, which makes the image larger. It also pulls the default PyPI `torch`, which brings CUDA libraries and adds several GB. A CPU-only torch index would shrink it considerably, but I didn't add one because I can't verify the wheel versions here.\n- **Runtime configuration:** no secrets are baked in. Pass them at run time, for example `--env-file .env`. The app starts without trained weights because it falls back to untrained demo weights, and `/api/health` reports `degraded` when config checks fail.\n\nWhen you build, watch the dependency install step first. It assumes Python 3.12 wheels exist for every pinned package on your architecture.",
